kMimic, a recipe that makes this training faster.\nL88: On a simulated Unitree G1, BlinkMimic trains one policy for all 40 LAFAN1 clips in 3.4 minutes on a single RTX 4090, measured until three consecutive checkpoints reach a normalized return of at least 0.82 with no failed clip (mean of three seeds). We split training time into the cost of an iteration, the iterations needed to fit the motions, and the iterations needed to remove the last failures, and assign each component, inherited or new, to one of these terms.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - HybridRobotics/supermimic: Humanoid whole-body motion tracking with one differentiable world model. · GitHub (https://github.com/HybridRobotics/supermimic)\nciteturn8view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/HybridRobotics/supermimic\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 270\nL0: 【0†Skip to content】\nL1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3:   * Products\nL4: \nL5:     *       * 【1†GitHub Repository hosting, code review, and collaboration】\nL6:       * 【2†Copilot AI coding agent for tasks, projects, and automated work】\nL7: \nL8:     * Build & Ship\nL9:       * 【3†Actions CI/CD and automation】\nL10:       * 【4†Code Quality Quality analysis, fixes, and enforcement】\nL11:       * 【5†Codespaces Cloud development environments】\nL12:     * Secure\nL13:       * 【6†Code Security Vulnerability detection and remediation】\nL14:       * 【7†Secret Protection Secret scanning and leak prevention】\nL15: \nL16: 【8†All Features】\nL17: \nL18:   * Developers\nL19: \nL20:     * Learn\nL21:       * 【9†Documentation†docs.github.com】\nL22:       * 【10†Training†learn.github.com】\nL23:       * 【11†Certifications†learn.github.com】\nL24: \nL25:     * Build\nL26:       * 【12†Build with Copilot】\nL27:       * 【13†Customize Copilot†docs.github.com】\nL28:       * 【14†Integrations】\nL29:     * Explore\nL30:       * 【15†Trending repos】\nL3